<title>USA: Vermont Supreme Court to hear property tax case.</title>
<headline>Vermont Supreme Court to hear property tax case.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Vermont Supreme Court will hear arguments this week on property tax reform in a suit filed by the American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU).</p>
<p>The ACLU charged  the state's system of funding education is unconstitutional because different communities have different amounts to spend. It is seeking a full trial.</p>
<p>The state, which wants the suit dismissed, argues that the Constitution does not guarantee equal education, or equal taxation.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
